libuv 1.48.0 for Cosmopolitan Libc (cosmocc), applied by hxc/tools/cosmo-deps.sh.

One Cosmopolitan binary runs on Linux, macOS, Windows and the BSDs, so libuv
is built as a generic unix port: the poll(2) backend (posix-poll.c, uv/posix.h
loop fields), with the platform files of the posix-poll ports (no-fsevents.c,
no-proctitle.c, posix-hrtime.c, bsd-ifaddrs.c, sysinfo-*.c) and the new
src/unix/cosmo.c for the rest (executable path, CPU count, RSS, uptime,
random bytes).

- uv/errno.h, uv-common.h: Cosmopolitan's errno constants (EAGAIN, ...) are
  variables holding the host OS's values, so they can't define the UV_E*
  enum. The UV__E* codes take the fixed values of libuv's Windows table and
  UV__ERR(errno) / uv_translate_sys_error translate at run time
  (uv__cosmo_err in cosmo.c). pipe.c: one bare -errno becomes UV__ERR(errno).
- random.c: uv_random through getrandom() (works on every host OS).
- uv-common.c, getaddrinfo.c: no if_nametoindex/if_indextoname in
  Cosmopolitan: numeric interface ids, as on Windows.
- udp.c: no source-specific multicast (as GNU/Hurd); SO_REUSEADDR for UDP
  reuse (SO_REUSEPORT means load balancing on Linux).
- bsd-ifaddrs.c: no AF_LINK hardware addresses (as GNU/Hurd).
- fs.c: futimens/utimensat for futime/lutime (as Linux).

